#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0121 expect=violation domain=ADLBC
#note "The BDS arm of the same rule - the sheet's second example ('BDS - APERSDT'). Expansion root 'APER' from both patterns; ONE tuple, ONE violation on row 1. APERSDT/APEREDT are real ADaMIG BDS 'Period, Subperiod, and Phase Start and End Timing' variables. Exercising two of the six declared structures is what keeps the multi-token Scope honest."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 APERSDT=22006 APEREDT=21950
dataset ADLBC structure=BDS
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col PARAMCD type=Char
col AVAL    type=Num
col APERSDT type=Num
col APEREDT type=Num
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | ALB | 3.5 | 22006 | 21950
